00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.640 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  one of the things that's been really  interesting about the tech companies of  the last you know 15 to 20 years is that  they've not only been innovating in  terms of their technology but also in  terms of their business models and  actually most of the successful tech  companies are some sort of platform  company their marketplaces like Amazon  matching buyers and sellers of products  or eBay they have advertising market  places like Google  all of these are platform companies and  so not only do they have to do technical  innovation but they also have to do  business and economic innovation there's  so many questions that come up in  operating these businesses as well as in  thinking about their strategy but just  have not been addressed before you can't  just you know call a consulting company  and say like what's the best practice  like I would for a factory if you're  operating a marketplace like an air B&amp;B  you have buyers consumers who want to  rent and you have sellers who are the  the owners of the homes the marketplace  has to really think about both sides of  the market on the sell side of the  market the home owners have to keep  their calendars current how annoying is  it to try to book a vacation home and  then have your reservation cancelled  because in a person says oops sorry my  calendar was wrong or wasn't available  so it's really important that the  suppliers in these marketplaces provide  a high-quality service keep their  calendars current answer questions  quickly provide good customer service  and good quality and they only do that  if they have the incentives to do so and  those incentives in turn are created by  the marketplace so there's a real  marketplace management challenge that's  new to these these tech marketplaces and  then the bigger platforms have strategic  considerations that are quite profound  especially because a lot of these  markets tend to be pretty concentrated  when you when you have a platform market  more buyers more sellers more sellers  more buyers more users more apps more  apps more users you don't have a lot of  opportunities to make mistakes and come  back later Microsoft was a little bit  late to the mobile phone market even  though they understood operating systems  been  than Google they missed the boat and so  they really have to get the strategy  right and understand all of the issues  about industry structure so we've seen  things like you know Google they created  a browser people like Google they're our  search engine how can they make a  browser but if you understand the  platform economics you understand why it  was really important for Google to have  a browser because the browser chooses  the default search engine and if people  are using your browser then the default  search engine will be your search engine  and that can be a really important  strategic advantage  so faced with all those those very  non-standard and quite challenging  problems most of the leading tech firms  have brought in not just sort of you  know macroeconomists who do forecasting  which is the traditional chief economist  type of role but they brought in micro  economists who think a lot more about  these strategic questions and also about  marketplace management and and pricing  policies and things like that  the evolution of a new tech firm is that  you have to start with an idea for a  product the next part is really  engineering you need to build the  product you need to deliver the product  and you need to incremental e make it  better until you get to some sort of  scale once you get to the point that you  then need to think about earning a  profit and becoming sustainable that's  really when the economics comes in and  so a lot of times that's a stage where a  firm will start trying to bring in this  expertise and of course you hire your  business people but often these problems  are so challenging and non-standard that  just a you know a generic business  background may not be enough and so  that's also a moment where the tech  economist can come in and bring in a  sort of academic perspective on it to be  able to design new systems to design the  reputation systems to design the pricing  systems to design an auction model if an  auction model is needed and so on and  they will change the companies by  teaching the engineers and teaching the  machine learning folks who might have  built the basic algorithms how to map  the business objectives onto their  engineering even determining what are  the goals what measures should be using  what KPI is should be using in business  lingo and it turns out that some  measurements that sound intuitive turn  out not to work very well for operating  a business they might be manipulable  they might not really represent  long-term success and so getting the  right measures that really capture the  organization's goals but still can be  measured in a timely fashion is  something that requires a lot of  economics and sort of business expertise  the tech firms really need economists  who can think about strategic questions  like industry structure that requires  understanding of sort of game theory and  industrial organization turns out that  you know some industry structures make  sense and some are really not  sustainable and then there's more of the  micro economic marketplace management if  you have a market place you know like a  Airbnb or like a Yelp which is a review  platform you need to really think about  the incentives of all the people  involved and you need to manage those  incentives so there's the economic  theory around what those incentives are  and designing and sent ofor all the  participants then there's also the  measurement we need to know how strong  those incentives have to be we need to  measure what the big problems are and we  design experiments that that test the  the impact of innovations and actually  designing experiments at a market place  is really quite difficult because  there's equilibrium effects if I I can't  just change things for 1% of the  suppliers and expect that to have the  same effect as if I change it for all  suppliers it's different of you and all  of your competitors experience a change  versus if just a single supplier  experiences that change by themselves  there are concerns about antitrust and  competition policy there are concerns  about privacy and security there are  concerns about new service providers how  do we think about you know regulating  the new Brewers and the lifts and so on  what are the rules that apply to these  new business models and so for all of  those types of questions the economists  role is to both conceptualize what are  the costs and benefits of what's going  on and also again to bring data to bear  the relationship between academia and  business has really changed with the  advent of tech firms historically there  was a bit of a divide you were an  academic or you were you know part of a  firm but because there's so many new  problems coming up in tech firms that  really require sort of cutting-edge  research and original thinking firms  have started plucking a very different  type of person into the into them  including putting a lot of emphasis on  very top academics and so how Varian was  you know the first example of this a  chief economist at Google Preston McAfee  went to to Yahoo and then I went to  Microsoft at the time that I spent time  at Microsoft I really got a lot of  pushback from my colleagues there was a  sense that well I had gone to do this  and I would never come back but I  understood that a huge part of my value  came from the types of skills I was  using in academics and so I was honing  my academic skills I was improving them  they taught me machine learning you know  they taught me a be testing the science  was more advanced inside the firm than  it was outside there was nothing like  that happening in academics at the time  now some people though have decided to  stay in in the tech firm careers and I  think one reason that academics are  happy there is that their jobs are  actually just really really interesting  they're doing the same quality of work  and the same rigor and challenge that  they would get in academics except for  the impact is immediate you're just  really seeing the the consequences of  your decisions much more quickly you  have control over the environment you  can build things at the beginning it was  pretty hard to bring in young people  newly minted economists and have them be  productive but as the groups have grown  it's there's now a career path and we're  seeing better and better young people  deciding to come into these jobs and  going to these tech firms can give them  the chance to do really rigorous  thinking and be really challenged  intellectually while changing products  and also living in an interdisciplinary  environment where they can learn new  skills from computer scientists and  engineers that they wouldn't have  interacted  otherwise  I think that economists are going to be  more attentive to the all of the social  science aspect and by the way other  social scientists are also contributing  and tech firms as well the behavioral  economics can really try to bring in the  perspective of what are the mistakes  consumers might make and how can I  design user interfaces or experiences to  help consumers make better decisions I  also think that when you see in a  marketplace say that you know a little  symbol that says the seller responds  within one hour to email requests or  even you know changes we've seen in the  review systems where instead of just  asking you for five stars they ask you  you know what is what was it that was  good here and they're careful about not  showing you the other person's review  until after you've put in your review a  lot of that is about economics and  incentives and trying to make sure that  the systems and the rules are set up so  that they provide the right incentives  for people to give the give honest  information and not retaliate and so on  so I think the the influence of the of  the economists are present and a lot of  those types of examples broadly then I  think what the economists are bringing  is sort of a way of thinking a way of  thinking about measurement a way of  thinking about the mapping of business  objectives to metrics and especially a  way of thinking about incentives  [Music]

